++Bottom line: the core asymptotic physics is sound, but commit `cae6a7d` does not yet close the planned frontier experiment.
++
++- `METHODOLOGY — FAIL.` The stack itself is standard: Ma-style channel/yields in [channel.py:60](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/qkdx/analytic/channel.py:60>), 1-decoy bounds in [analytic/decoy.py:30](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/qkdx/analytic/decoy.py:30>), and GLLP/WLC composition in [decoy.py:111](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/qkdx/numerics/decoy.py:111>). The flaw is the comparison design: the claimed “Pareto degradation” is evaluated at fixed `μ=0.5, ν=0.1` in [findings.md:22](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:22>) and [findings.md:37](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:37>); only LMC gets a μ sweep at [findings.md:79](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:79>). That supports an operating-point result, not a frontier result.
++
++- `FINDING STRENGTH — PASS.` The `80–87%` number is supported by the committed tables/raw data in [findings.md:41](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:41>) and [json:110](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.json:110>). Supplementary reruns on this commit show `η_d` loss alone gives about `50%` degradation; adding `e_misalignment=0.033` drives it to about `83–87%`; `p_d=1e-6` is secondary until the longest distances. So the main mechanism is `η_d` drop plus misalignment, not dark count. Coarse joint `μ,ν` re-optimization still stayed in the same band.
++
++- `LIMITATIONS — FAIL.` Finite-size and 2-decoy are already covered in [findings.md:107](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:107>) and [findings.md:109](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:109>). Missing caveats are: no explicit “no joint per-profile `(distance, μ, ν)` optimization” disclaimer, and the claimed raw `205`-point 2-D sweep is not actually archived: [PHASE1_LOG.md:88](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/PHASE1_LOG.md:88>) vs [json:132](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.json:132>). PDC/Fock-state source is not a missing limitation here; it is outside this coherent-decoy BB84 scope.
++
++- `PLAN ALIGNMENT — FAIL.` The hard scan requirement remains open: the plan wants `≥1000` points at [RESEARCH_PLAN.md:279](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/RESEARCH_PLAN.md:279>), while the delivery logs only `262` evaluated points and admits the gap at [PHASE1_LOG.md:100](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/PHASE1_LOG.md:100>). The test at [test_decoy_bb84_sweep.py:93](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/tests/test_sweeps/test_decoy_bb84_sweep.py:93>) proves code capability, not experiment completion. Plan inputs/outputs at [RESEARCH_PLAN.md:286](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/RESEARCH_PLAN.md:286>) are also not fully closed.
++
++- `SCOPE DISCIPLINE — FAIL.` The delivery drifts into acceptance rewriting/partial-close language in [findings.md:58](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:58>), [findings.md:101](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:101>), and [PHASE1_LOG.md:104](</Users/tengjun/Desktop/ai4qkd (1)/AI4QKD/docs/PHASE1_LOG.md:104>). Reporting the mismatch is in scope; redefining the target is not.
