ger says the current tests validate the optimized comparison unless they actually do."},{"severity":"major","category":"correctness","location":"docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:8; docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections.md:128; docs/findings/s2.3_device_imperfections_r2.json:214","description":"The delivery claims the `1221`-point TYPICAL_S23 sweep is archived in JSON as a 'complete scan', but the new `full_1000pt_sweep_TYPICAL_S23` object stores only `n_points`, coarse grid parameters, and a 19-point `upper_envelope_sample`. The underlying 37×33 sweep data or raw Pareto points are not present, so the archive does not actually preserve the claimed experiment artifact. That means the specific plan-alignment check '1221-point sweep archived in json' is still not closed.","suggestion":"Serialize the full sweep into the JSON artifact, for example as axes plus a rate matrix or as a flat list of `{distance_km, mu, nu, rate}` records, and keep the current envelope sample only as a convenience summary. Then align the findings/log wording with what is actually stored."}],"round_recommendation":"Tighten the S2.3 regression tests to check the documented degradation bands on the intended optimized/fixed basis, and archive the full 1221-point sweep data rather than just a count and sample. After those two gaps are closed, this round should be ready to re-review."}
